"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1571283/000157128326000051/rexr-20260916.htm"},{"date":"2026-09-11","sym":"AMH","name":"American Homes 4 Rent Common Shares of Beneficial Interest","form":"SCHEDULE 13D","what":"A large holder disclosed a stake and its intentions (13D)","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1562401/000119312526389440/xslSCHEDULE_13D_X02/primary_doc.xml"},{"date":"2026-09-11","sym":"AMH","name":"American Homes 4 Rent Common Shares of Beneficial Interest","form":"SCHEDULE 13D/A","what":"A large holder disclosed a stake and its intentions (13D)","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1562401/000119312526389436/xslSCHEDULE_13D_X02/primary_doc.xml"},{"date":"2026-09-01","sym":"RHP","name":"Ryman Hospitality Properties Inc. (REIT)","form":"8-K","what":"Completed an acquisition or sale of assets","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1040829/000110465926104349/tm2624390d1_8k.htm"}],"companies":62,"days":60,"ok":true},"story":[{"tone":"warn","text":"A 30-year fixed mortgage costs 7.32% this week, versus 6.27% a year ago. It is up from four weeks ago (7.03%)."},{"tone":"warn","text":"On a median-priced home ($410,700) with 20% down, the monthly payment for the loan alone (principal and interest) is about $2,257, versus about $2,054 a year ago. At the lowest rate in the last five years (2.88% in 2021) it would be about $1,222, a difference of $1,035 a month."},{"tone":"info","text":"Home prices (Case-Shiller, through 2026-07) are +1.9% from a year ago. Prices move slowly and lag mortgage rates by months."},{"tone":"info","text":"Existing homes are selling at a pace of 3.99 million a year, -2.2% from a year ago. High rates tend to freeze the market: owners with cheap old mortgages don't want to sell."},{"tone":"warn","text":"There are 8.5 months of new homes for sale at the current pace. That is above the ~6 months seen in a balanced market, which usually means builders must offer discounts or incentives."},{"tone":"info","text":"Builders pulled permits at a 1,400 thousand yearly pace and started homes at 1,221 thousand (permits -3.0% vs a year ago). Permits come first, so they show where building is heading."},{"tone":"info","text":"Markets: homebuilder stocks (ITB) are -10.4% over three months and real estate funds (VNQ) -7.7%. Stocks often move ahead of the housing data because investors look forward."}],"disclaimer":"Facts from Freddie Mac, the St. Louis Fed (FRED), Yahoo Finance and SEC EDGAR. Educational only; not investment advice."}